WEBVTT

1
00:00.000 --> 00:12.000
KYVERA is a decentralized identity-continuity protocol for BCH and Nostr.

2
00:12.000 --> 00:30.000
Create a binding with two independent keys. No server holds the identity.

3
00:30.000 --> 00:50.000
The Trust Challenge runs Bind, Verify, Authenticate, Rotate and Prove with real verifier logic.

4
00:50.000 --> 01:10.000
Authentication uses a fresh, single-use challenge and a short-lived relying-party session.

5
01:10.000 --> 01:30.000
Rotation requires the old wallet, the new wallet and the Nostr key.

6
01:30.000 --> 01:50.000
Historical proof remains valid after rotation; current authorization moves.

7
01:50.000 --> 02:10.000
The merchant demo updates its payment destination only after verification.

8
02:10.000 --> 02:25.000
The standalone relying party verifies the same public protocol without KYVERA's website.

9
02:25.000 --> 02:41.000
Fail-closed policy blocks partial or stale relay states. Real-wallet and public-relay interoperability remain untested.
